# AGENTS.md

Guidance for AI coding agents (Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, Codex, and
similar) working in this repository. Read this file first, then the rule files
it points to. The rules are short so that they fit in context; follow them
exactly so your changes survive `cleanstack regenerate`.

## Read before writing code

1. [.ai/rules/architecture.md](.ai/rules/architecture.md) — layers and allowed dependencies
2. [.ai/rules/naming-conventions.md](.ai/rules/naming-conventions.md) — the naming contract
3. [.ai/rules/protected-regions.md](.ai/rules/protected-regions.md) — how to edit generated files safely
4. [.ai/rules/adding-an-entity.md](.ai/rules/adding-an-entity.md) — workflow for new entities
5. [ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md) — full-stack architecture overview

## Workspace layout

```text
{{kebabCase project.name}}/
  {{kebabCase project.name}}-backend/    Spring Boot REST API{{#if project.options.frontend}}
  {{kebabCase project.name}}-ui/         Angular single-page application{{/if}}
  entities/         Entity descriptors (YAML), the source of truth for CRUD code
  .ai/              Agent rules (load these before generating code)
  .cleanstack/      Generator metadata (read-only for agents)
```

## Golden rules

1. **Generated code is owned by the generator.** Files produced by CleanStack
   may only be modified inside `<cleanstack:user-code>` regions. Hand edits
   anywhere else are destroyed by the next regeneration. Details:
   [.ai/rules/protected-regions.md](.ai/rules/protected-regions.md).
2. **Derive names from the entity.** Every artifact name comes from the entity
   name via the table in
   [.ai/rules/naming-conventions.md](.ai/rules/naming-conventions.md). Never
   invent a new naming style.
3. **Do not hand-write CRUD.** New entities are a YAML descriptor plus
   `cleanstack entity <Name>`, which generates the
   {{#if project.options.frontend}}backend and frontend{{else}}backend{{/if}} artifacts
   consistently. Hand-written code belongs in protected regions or new files
   you create yourself.
4. **Respect the layers.** Dependencies point from the edges (controllers,
   pages) toward the domain. See
   [.ai/rules/architecture.md](.ai/rules/architecture.md).
5. **Verify before finishing.** Backend changes must pass
   {{#if (eq project.options.buildTool "maven")}}`mvn clean verify`{{else}}`gradle clean build`{{/if}}.{{#if project.options.frontend}}
   Frontend changes must pass `npm test` and `npm start` in
   `{{kebabCase project.name}}-ui`.{{/if}}
   Template-affecting changes: run `cleanstack regenerate --dry-run` first.

